# Phase-1 SEO (built in from day 0)

## A) URL & content model

* **Canonical, stable URLs**

  * Product: `/p/{slug}` (primary) with an ID alias `/p/{id}` that 301s to the slug.
  * Home list: `/`
* **KV additions per product**

  * `slug` (required, immutable once live), `seoTitle`, `seoDescription`, `imageAlt`, optional `brand`, `sku|mpn|gtin`, `currency`, `availability` (“InStock”, etc.)

## B) Page-level SEO (SSR via Fresh `Head`)

* **Titles**

  * Home: “{Brand} — {Short Value Prop}”
  * Product: “{Product Name} | {Brand}”
* **Meta description**

  * 140–160 chars; product page pulls from `seoDescription` (fallback to truncated description).
* **Canonical link**

  * Home → `/`; product → `/p/{slug}`; add canonical to avoid any dupes.
* **Indexation rules**

  * Public pages: index/follow.
  * Auth-only endpoints, cart, checkout, admin: `noindex, nofollow`.

## C) Structured data (JSON-LD, SSR)

* **Product** on product pages:

  * `@type: Product` with `name`, `image`, `description`, `sku|mpn|gtin` (if available), `brand` (if available).
  * `offers`: `@type: Offer`, `price`, `priceCurrency`, `availability`, `url`.
  * (Optional) `aggregateRating` only when real data exists.
* **ItemList** on home:

  * `@type: ItemList` with list of product `url`s and positions.
* **BreadcrumbList** for product pages:

  * Home → Product (two-level only; clean and minimal).

## D) Social previews (Open Graph & Twitter Cards)

* **Open Graph (important for Facebook audience)**

  * `og:type` `product` on product pages; `website` on home.
  * `og:title`, `og:description`, `og:url`, `og:image` (≥1200×630; JPG/PNG; absolute URL).
  * `fb:app_id` (use your Facebook App ID for Insights).
* **Twitter**

  * `twitter:card` `summary_large_image`, plus `title`, `description`, `image`.

## E) Crawling, sitemaps, robots

* **`/robots.txt`**

  * Allow `/` and `/p/`; Disallow `/cart`, `/checkout`, `/orders`, `/api/*`, `/auth/*`, `/admin/*`.
  * Point to sitemap: `Sitemap: https://{domain}/sitemap.xml`
* **`/sitemap.xml`** (SSR route)

  * Home + all products; update daily (or on product change) with `<lastmod>`.
* **HTTP**

  * Force HTTPS, add HSTS. 301 any `www`/non-canonical hosts to primary.

## F) Performance & CWV (ships in Phase-1)

* **SSR by default**: bots get full HTML.
* **Critical practices**

  * Set explicit `width`/`height` on images to avoid CLS.
  * Lazy-load below-the-fold images; preload hero image.
  * Cache policy:

    * HTML: short TTL (e.g., 60–120s) with ETag; revalidate on product edits.
    * Static images: long TTL (e.g., 30d) with fingerprinted URLs.
* **Edge hints**

  * `rel=preconnect` to image host (if external).
  * Keep JS tiny (Fresh islands already help).

## G) Internationalization & locale (v1-ready)

* Single-language v1: set `html lang` (e.g., `en` or `bn`) and `og:locale` accordingly.
* Plan for `hreflang` if/when multilingual launches (Phase-2).

## H) Admin inputs (to make SEO non-blocking)

* Add fields to the simple admin editor:

  * `slug` (validated unique; URL preview)
  * `seoTitle` (counter to \~60 chars)
  * `seoDescription` (counter to \~160 chars)
  * `imageAlt`
  * (Optional) `brand`, `sku|mpn|gtin`, `availability`, `currency`

## I) Tracking & privacy (lightweight)

* Basic server logs/aggregates are enough for Phase-1.
* If you add any pixels later, ensure they’re behind consent and don’t affect CLS.

## J) Acceptance criteria (Phase-1 now includes)

* Each product page renders SSR with unique **title**, **meta description**, **canonical**, **Open Graph**, **Twitter Card**, and **Product JSON-LD** (valid in Rich Results).
* Home page renders **ItemList JSON-LD** with links to all active products.
* **Sitemap** includes all active product URLs with `lastmod` and is referenced by **robots.txt**.
* Non-public pages return `noindex` and are excluded from sitemap.
* All product images specify width/height, pass Lighthouse CLS budget; HTML pages return 200 with canonical set.
* OG share for a product (via Facebook debugger) shows correct title/description/image.
* `slug` immutability is enforced once a product goes live (or old slug 301s to new).

